for me  joking about suicide is not something  that i do uh on the show  and i am not someone who says here's a  list of topics you can never joke about  but on this program we we do sometimes  joke about things but i don't joke about  suicide  uh and it makes it all the more  um  interesting  that the ukrainian ambassador to the  united nations sergey  yesterday said in a serious way again  without joking about suicide if putin  wants to end up dead  he should just shoot himself dead the  way hitler did in the bunker in 1945 and  the point here  is actually it's not a joke it's if for  whatever reason putin has a death wish  the desire to destroy  reckless uh  reckless desires which could lead to him  ending up dead  don't  kill other people just kill yourself and  that's me paraphrasing let's listen to  sergey kislytsia yesterday to the united  nations we have been prompted to call  for an emergency special session as the  level of the threat to the global  security has been equated to the to that  of the second world war  or even higher following  putin's order to put an alert russian  nuclear forces what what a madness  if he wants to kill himself  he doesn't need to use nuclear arsenal  he has to do what he's saying what what  the guy in in berlin did in the bunker  in may  1945. so of course he's referring to  hitler taking his own life and i think  there is a point here that is a good one  if vladimir putin has a death wish if he  wants to blow everything up proverbially  as much as literally and end up dead  potentially he could just take himself  out and not as many other people i don't  think this is a joke about suicide it's  not a question of encouraging suicide or  any of it the sentiment that comes  through here is if you're determined to  ruin your own life why do you have to  ruin so many others as well i was  watching video on argentinian television  this morning  they have correspondence on the border  between ukraine and poland and to see  the looks of shock on people's faces as  they flee ukraine some literally unable  to speak for periods of time  from the shock that they are  experiencing you you don't have to ruin  other people's lives if you're simply  determined to ruin your own now to some  degree  i would bet anything i have  that the topic of assassinating putin  has come up at the top levels of  government i'm not saying anyone's  thinking of doing it i'm not saying  anyone plans to do it or would do it but  without a doubt  when aids are supposed to present all  options to world leaders  it is impossible to imagine that they  are coming forward and saying okay we  can send weapons we could send troops we  could look at drones we can do this we  can do that  here's what it would look like if we  tried to assassinate putin it's clearly  being mentioned by the people who were  paid to present all options to world  leaders i don't believe it's being  seriously considered i don't believe  it's going to be done and i'm not  suggesting it be done but the point here  from the ukrainian ambassador once again  is  not everybody has to suffer because  putin has become a reckless tyrant and  uh that certainly is coming through in  the desperation  of the voice of the ambassador from  ukraine to the united nations

